description:
PRINCIPAL ACCOUNTABILITIES
The following aspects of this role are indicative only and in no way limit the Company in allocating additional or alternate accountabilities (specific tasks, projects or related activities) to the employee, within the scope of the employee’s level of competence, experience, knowledge and qualification.
RESPONSIBILITIES
(1) Responsible for departmental daily data processing, report preparation & submission, analysis and workflow automation;
(2) Assist the Department to optimise and existing reporting to improve data & reporting quality, maintenance of related models, data & system and workflow automation;
(3) Support the Department Credit Admin function to assist in finance documents review, credit limit & system maintenance, post approval credit monitoring and portfolio management;
(4) Assist in comprehensive risk management including monitoring various risk indicators, identify potential risks and provide early warnings and analysis;
(5) Coordinate and support Audit, Regulatory inspections and risk-related projects such as risk culture, business continuity plan and testing;
(6) Providing other ad hoc administrative support to the Risk Management Department’s daily operations.
EXPERIENCE, QUALIFICATIONS SKILLS & ABILITIES
· Undergraduate degree in Commerce, Business, Data Analytics, Computer Science or other related business studies;
· 3 years’ experience in Risk Management, Reporting & Analysis or Credit Administration, ideally with a Bank or Financial Institution;
· Good command of English and Chinese;
· Sound analytical skills with high level accuracy and attention to detail;
· Good communicator, both verbally and in writing to the level of business report writing;
· Effective time management and good organisational skills;
· Ability to interpret and follow procedures;
· Advanced skills in Microsoft Excel, Word, SQL / VBA or others;
· Good interpersonal skills and good team player.
